WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.176
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambridge exams.

2
00:00:05.476 --> 00:00:08.944
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.244 --> 00:00:18.026
Unit three: A2 Key: Writing Messages and Picture Stories. Today you will write a short email and a story about three pictures.

4
00:00:18.326 --> 00:00:20.839
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.928
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.783 --> 00:00:26.842
Message.

7
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:30.778
Message means a short piece of writing sent to someone.

8
00:00:31.383 --> 00:00:32.953
Write a short message.

9
00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.040
Your turn. Say: Message.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:39.878
Message.

11
00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:41.606
Invite.

12
00:00:42.617 --> 00:00:44.965
Invite means to ask someone to come.

13
00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:47.259
I invite you to my party.

14
00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.502
Your turn. Say: Invite.

15
00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:54.228
Invite.

16
00:00:54.983 --> 00:00:55.950
Suggest.

17
00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:59.112
Suggest means to give an idea.

18
00:00:59.717 --> 00:01:01.589
I suggest meeting at six.

19
00:01:02.183 --> 00:01:04.603
Your turn. Say: Suggest.

20
00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:08.433
Suggest.

21
00:01:09.183 --> 00:01:10.173
Because.

22
00:01:11.183 --> 00:01:13.241
Because means used to give a reason.

23
00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:15.884
I am happy because it is Friday.

24
00:01:16.483 --> 00:01:18.915
Your turn. Say: Because.

25
00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:22.745
Because.

26
00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:24.159
Then.

27
00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:26.581
Then means after that.

28
00:01:27.183 --> 00:01:28.382
Then we went home.

29
00:01:28.983 --> 00:01:31.183
Your turn. Say: Then.

30
00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:34.872
Then.

31
00:01:35.617 --> 00:01:36.455
Finally.

32
00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:39.020
Finally means at the end.

33
00:01:39.617 --> 00:01:41.047
Finally, we ate lunch.

34
00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:44.186
Your turn. Say: Finally.

35
00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:47.860
Finally.

36
00:01:48.617 --> 00:01:49.827
Picture story.

37
00:01:50.817 --> 00:01:53.722
Picture story means a story based on three pictures.

38
00:01:54.317 --> 00:01:55.863
Write a picture story.

39
00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:59.218
Your turn. Say: Picture story.

40
00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:03.288
Picture story.

41
00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:05.132
Past simple.

42
00:02:06.117 --> 00:02:08.917
Past simple means the tense for finished actions.

43
00:02:09.517 --> 00:02:10.982
We visited the beach.

44
00:02:11.583 --> 00:02:14.410
Your turn. Say: Past simple.

45
00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:18.918
Past simple.

46
00:02:19.733 --> 00:02:23.164
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.017 --> 00:02:26.353
Visal, what are the two writing tasks?

48
00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:40.087
In Part 6 you write an email of about twenty-five words and answer three points. In Part 7 you write a story of about thirty-five words about three pictures.

49
00:02:41.183 --> 00:02:42.672
How do I write the email?

50
00:02:43.783 --> 00:02:54.795
Answer every point in the question. For example, if you must say when you can meet, where you want to go and why, write one short sentence for each point.

51
00:02:55.883 --> 00:02:57.546
How do I write the story?

52
00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:08.628
Use the past simple and sequence words like first, then and finally. Give names to the people, and write a sentence for each picture.

53
00:03:09.767 --> 00:03:11.325
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:12.183 --> 00:03:16.249
Grammar focus: Strategy: cover every point, keep it simple.

55
00:03:16.549 --> 00:03:17.736
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:21.285
I can meet you on Saturday because I am free in the morning.

57
00:03:22.183 --> 00:03:24.833
First, Ben went to the park; then he met his friends.

58
00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:34.503
Read the instructions, cover every point and write simple, correct sentences. For stories, use the past simple and one sentence per picture.

59
00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:38.761
Be careful! Don't say: I forget one point in the email.

60
00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:42.804
Say: I answer every point.

61
00:03:43.104 --> 00:03:44.384
Cover every point.

62
00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.968
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:50.046
A Picture Story.

64
00:03:50.346 --> 00:03:52.706
The three pictures show a boy called Ben.

65
00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.141
In the first picture Ben goes to the park.

66
00:03:57.133 --> 00:03:59.609
In the second picture he meets his friends.

67
00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.319
In the third picture they play football together.

68
00:04:04.333 --> 00:04:06.646
Ben writes a sentence for each picture.

69
00:04:07.733 --> 00:04:11.689
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:15.327
The email in Part 6 is about blank words.

71
00:04:15.627 --> 00:04:20.035
A, 25. B, 250. C, 2.

72
00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:25.925
The answer is A: 25.

73
00:04:27.083 --> 00:04:29.106
Which tense is best for the story?

74
00:04:29.406 --> 00:04:33.721
A, imperative. B, past simple. C, future perfect.

75
00:04:37.267 --> 00:04:39.522
The answer is B: past simple.

76
00:04:40.683 --> 00:04:42.091
'Then' is a word for blank.

77
00:04:42.391 --> 00:04:45.812
A, place. B, colour. C, sequence.

78
00:04:49.367 --> 00:04:51.169
The answer is C: sequence.

79
00:04:52.317 --> 00:04:54.397
In the third picture the friends blank.

80
00:04:54.697 --> 00:04:57.887
A, play football. B, study. C, cook.

81
00:05:01.433 --> 00:05:04.129
The answer is A: play football.

82
00:05:05.283 --> 00:05:07.492
You must answer blank in the email.

83
00:05:07.792 --> 00:05:11.724
A, no points. B, every point. C, one point.

84
00:05:15.267 --> 00:05:17.382
The answer is B: every point.

85
00:05:18.567 --> 00:05:21.718
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:22.583 --> 00:05:25.906
How do you write a short email in the A2 Key exam?

87
00:05:34.717 --> 00:05:36.252
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:36.552 --> 00:05:48.228
I read the instructions and underline the points that I must answer. I write one short sentence for each point with simple grammar. At the end I check spelling and capital letters.

89
00:05:48.528 --> 00:05:50.109
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:56.769
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: cover every point, keep it simple.

91
00:05:57.069 --> 00:06:01.393
Today's value is communication. Speak clearly and listen carefully.

92
00:06:01.693 --> 00:06:04.183
See you in Unit four. Goodbye!

93
00:06:04.483 --> 00:06:07.286
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

